    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3). The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional 4-digit `postcode` to owners, validated against the city's region per the fixed table, and stored/returned when present.\n\n**Contract & validation**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (`pattern: \"^[0-9]{4}$\"`, **not** in `required`). The generated DTO's `@Pattern` makes a malformed value (e.g. `\"12\"`) a 400 via the existing `ValidationExceptionHandler`, and inheritance means it's also part of the `Owner` response DTO.\n- `RequirePostcodeForCity` (new function) \u2014 the region range check. Validates **only when present**; a city with no known region (range `null`) accepts any 4-digit postcode; an out-of-range value throws the checked `PostcodeOutOfRangeException`.\n- `PostcodeOutOfRangeException` + `...Handler` + escalation YAML \u2014 respond 400 with the `{ \"errors\": [\"postcode\"] }` shape used by the sibling telephone handler.\n- `Localities.postcodeRange(city)` \u2014 the fixed region\u2192range table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) kept alongside the existing city\u2192region table.\n\n**Wiring & persistence**\n- Wired the `postcode` step into `owners.POST.yml` (after address normalization) and `{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (after validate), inside the transaction governance.\n- `Owner` entity \u2014 new `postcode` column + accessors; `ApplyOwner` now sets it on update; MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions.\n- Added the `postcode` column to all four schema dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\nThe three new acceptance tests (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`) and the full suite pass.",
